WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.943
In about a minute, you will find the lights and events near you.

00:00:03.943 --> 00:00:05.033
We start on the map.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:09.220
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.108 --> 00:00:13.540
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.039
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:17.389
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.174 --> 00:00:21.543
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.543 --> 00:00:22.240
Tap Allow.

00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:25.944
The map zooms to where you are.

00:00:25.944 --> 00:00:30.038
There are no events on your street, so tap Show all of Southern California.

00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:37.126
Now every place shows how far away it is, nearest first, so you can plan your drive.

00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:40.134
Choose a season.

00:00:40.134 --> 00:00:42.057
Tap the season button at the top.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.241
Tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:00:48.063 --> 00:00:49.421
Or search for a city.

00:00:49.421 --> 00:00:51.766
Type its name, and tap it in the list.

00:00:55.919 --> 00:00:59.367
To drive to what you see, tap Route these, under the list.

00:01:01.397 --> 00:01:04.371
A long list is split into routes of nine or fewer.

00:01:04.371 --> 00:01:09.152
Each route starts where the last one ended, and you can tick off places as you go.

00:01:10.846 --> 00:01:12.960
To narrow the list, tap Filters.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.163
You can pick a date, a distance, a type, and more.

00:01:18.513 --> 00:01:20.812
That is how you find lights near you.

00:01:20.812 --> 00:01:25.410
Use your location, pick a season, search a city, and narrow it with Filters.

00:01:26.809 --> 00:01:28.888
Next up: Plan a night.
